	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Since the age of Netheril, mages have learned to bestow a wide variety of magical properties upon the everyday objects that surround them. A favorite item of such enchantment is the common robe. It is lightweight, affordable, and holds its enchantment well, thereby making it ideal equipment for a mage. Due to their magical heritage, however, only single-, dual-, and multi-class mages may wear these enchanted robes.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 3"

	SAY NAME2 "Robe of the Shattered One"
	SAY DESC "This flowing vestment once belonged to Jon Irenicus. Embroidered across the chest is a broken circle in faded elven gold runes, symbolizing his exile from Suldanessellar and his severed connection to the Tree of Life. The robe emanates an aura of cold arrogance and immense power, visibly distorting reality around the wearer. The corrupted essence imprinted within the fabric protects the user from any form of spiritual manipulation and spatial banishment, leaving the wearer's magic untethered and amplified.

